# Regression: agents watching the stage must move during exodus.
# Previously WatchingStage wasn't removed, so agents turned blue but froze.
#
# HARDENING (2026-10-18): this script used to fail ~1 in 3 full-suite runs.
# Root cause: `wait 5` after spawning gave agents only ~2.5 tiles of
# travel (0.5 tiles/s on StageFloor) to reach their assigned stage spot,
# but spawn targets are RANDOM StageFloor spots (best_stage_spot picks
# from a band around the stage), and some targets sit on the far side of
# the 4x4 Stage building, requiring a walk around it (~12 tiles). Watching
# only starts on the EXACT target tile, so with 5s none of the 10 agents
# had necessarily arrived yet. reset_game does NOT reseed the shared RNG,
# so full-suite runs draw different targets than standalone runs — hence
# flaky in suite, stable standalone.
# Fixes (test-side only; no game-code change). Custom `assert_*` commands
# fail on first evaluation (no retry), so the margin comes from wait
# length — the pattern stable movement scripts use (e.g. 21_stage_entry):
# - WEAKENED (timing only, not the assertion): the pre-watch wait is now
#   15s instead of 5s, i.e. 7.5 tiles of travel budget. Spots on the near
#   side of the ring are only a few tiles away, so at least one of the 10
#   agents arrives well within the window. 15s is still under the minimum
#   30s watch duration and the minimum 30s need threshold (need timers
#   also freeze while watching), so early watchers have not stopped
#   watching and no agent has been pulled away by a need yet. The assert
#   itself stays `gte 1` — the weakest existence form.
# - NOT weakened: the exodus assert stays exact (`eq 0`) — exactness is
#   the regression under test. It is not timing-marginal: ExodusSystem
#   clears WatchingStage in the first frame of exodus, and it runs after
#   the goal system each frame, so want cannot flip back to Stage and
#   watching cannot be re-added. The post-exodus wait is widened from
#   `wait_frames 5` to `wait 1` anyway, giving the transition a full
#   sim-second instead of a frame count.
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
wait_frames 5

# Spawn agents on StageFloor (outside the 4x4 stage building at 30-33,25-28
# but within STAGE_WATCH_RADIUS=8 of center 32,27)
spawn_agents 28 27 5 stage
spawn_agents 35 27 5 stage

# Wait for at least one agent to reach its (random) stage spot and start
# watching (see header: 15s = 7.5 tiles of travel budget).
wait 15

# Confirm agents are watching the stage
assert_agent_watching gte 1

# Trigger exodus
set_time 0 0
assert_phase exodus
wait 1

# All agents should have WatchingStage removed immediately.
# If the bug regresses, they stay WatchingStage and freeze in place.
assert_agent_watching eq 0
